# Traundl: the lake's flat-bottomed Plaette (Traunerl), rowed standing
# (moving platform, D-077, the Gondel's free-running ping-pong). A long dark
# wooden hull o/O/l with a k outline: the raised, upturned bow on the LEFT
# (the real boat's landing ramp; pointed, rising 4 px above the deck only in
# x 0-4), the raked stern on the right with the oar blade and w ripples in
# the corner. The rower stands at the stern (x 34-45, rows 0-15): a local in
# shirt sleeves w/i, a green G/j hat, d breeches, with the long oar O.
#
# Walking surface: row 16 (k edge, o gunwale lip at row 17) across all
# 48 px; the hitbox is the 48x16 body (rows 16-31). Nothing below row 31.
# Built with a throwaway script, frozen here; the grids are the source.
sprite = traundl
size   = 48x32
origin = 24,32
hitbox = 0,16,48,16
mirror = auto
anim   = idle frames=2 ticks=30 loop
anim   = ride frames=2 ticks=12 loop
